<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · text</p><h1 class="enc-title">Book of Jeremiah</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Book of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jeremiah">Jeremiah</a> is a book of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hebrew-bible">Hebrew Bible</a> containing the prophecies and life of Jeremiah, who was active in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/judah">Judah</a> from the late seventh century BCE until after the Babylonian <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/siege-of-jerusalem-587-bce">destruction of Jerusalem in 587</a> BCE. It calls on the kingdoms of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mount-ararat">Ararat</a>, Minni and Ashkenaz to rise against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/babylon">Babylon</a>, a late reference to the region of Urartu. By word count it is the longest book of the Bible.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/book-of-jeremiah.jpg" alt="Book of Jeremiah" width="320" height="318" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Daderot · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Stamp_seal_with_Hebrew_text_of_Jeremiah_48-11,_probably_early_centuries_AD,_terracotta_-_Oriental_Institute_Museum,_University_of_Chicago_-_DSC07746.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
